403519750337,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":43.9,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.5763937586448729,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.13484878396246755,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":61.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.006625312239589259,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":35.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.08199809074586817,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":82.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.036659621897982754,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":51.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.004711844668816356,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":44.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009170072729458436,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.14505,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":96.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Accel Entertainment, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a distributed gaming operator in the United States. It engages in the installation, maintenance, and operation of gaming terminals; redemption devices that disburse winnings and contain automated teller machine (ATM) functionality; and other amusement devices in authorized non-casino locations, such as restaurants, bars, taverns, convenience stores, liquor stores, truck stops, and grocery stores. The company also designs and manufactures gaming terminals and related equipment, as well as offers turnkey and full-service gaming solutions to bars, restaurants, convenience stores, truck stops, and fraternal and veteran establishments. In addition, it operates stand-alone ATMs in gaming and non-gaming locations, as well as amusement devices, including jukeboxes, dartboards, pool tables, and other entertainment related equipment; and develops brick-and-mortar casinos that serve local gaming markets and horse racing venues. Accel Entertainment, Inc. is headquartered in Burr Ridge, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark T. Phelan | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $872,706 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $832K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $39K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Accel Entertainment, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.1B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 7% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $62M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.93\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.22001471670346007},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 8% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 66% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Accel Entertainment (NYSE:ACEL) versus Rush Street Interactive (NYSE:RSI) Financial Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/accel-entertainment-nyseacel-versus-rush-street-interactive-nysersi-financial-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566814.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.967,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Earnings Strength Altering The Investment Case For Accel Enterta